{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Bread of affliction.</b> Bread that recalls the affliction that we endured in Egypt (Sifrei)." "<b>For in haste you departed.</b> The dough did not have time to leaven — and this shall be for you a remembrance. And the haste was not yours but the Egyptians', as it says: ״וַתֶּחֱזַק מִצְרַיִם עַל הָעָם וְגוֹ׳״ (Sifrei)." "<b>So that you remember.</b> Through eating the paschal offering and the matzah <b>the day of your departure</b>."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:16.612408170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}